IMPORT prelude
IMPORT properties

-- D3, with Bob's purchase recorded and then cancelled: the fixture pair for
-- the instance ledger's strict mode (OPERATIONAL-LOWERING-SPEC section 2,
-- ruling R-O4). An operational-lowering fixture only; the brief's d1, d2
-- and d3 have no cancellation, and a cancel act there is the d3-cancel
-- mutant, which is a different act (it cancels Alice's dinner).
--
-- Alice checks whether dinner is bought at 18:05 and reads the dinner
-- status record with one entry, opened. Then Bob's purchase is recorded
-- (taken, at 18:06) and Bob cancels it (opened again, at 18:06:30), both
-- between Alice's read and her buy at 18:07. Dinner is unbought again, so
-- the rule lets Alice buy: the trace below ends with one dinner, accepted
-- while open. That is the ledger's default, the semantic guard.
--
-- The ledger's strict mode is the version-number discipline on top of it:
-- the record's version is the count of its recorded status events, not of
-- the distinct states, so it moved from one, when Alice read it, to three,
-- and a strict proposal of the same buy is refused as a conflict, nothing
-- appended. Strictness is the ledger's, not the rule's, so no trace here
-- can show it; the ledger's tests (jl4-core/test/LedgerSpec.hs) drive both
-- proposals.
--
-- Same shape as d3-atomic.l4, with two changes. Bob's cancellation is an
-- act. And every reading of the record takes its latest entry: the
-- brief's `the ledger's status` (properties.l4) treats a record that ever
-- held `taken` as taken for good, which is right for the brief, where
-- nothing reopens, and would refuse Alice's buy here.

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `ledger records Bob's purchase`            -- BobBuys
    `ledger records Bob's cancellation`        -- the record reopens
    `Messages delivers the message`            -- Deliver
    `Alice checks whether dinner is bought`    -- CheckBought
    `Alice is done`                            -- Done
    `Alice buys dinner`                        -- BuyChecked if answered, NoAnswer if not
        HAS `ledger answered` IS A BOOLEAN

`closing` MEANS 75600

§ `Reading the latest status`

-- Every reader takes the cell's value as its input, and the call site does
-- the RECALL (README.md of the brief, "Traps").
GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A Status
`the latest status` MEANS
    CONSIDER reverse `dinner status record`
    WHEN EMPTY                      THEN opened
    WHEN latest FOLLOWED BY earlier THEN latest

GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`dinner is open now` MEANS `the latest status` `dinner status record` EQUALS opened

§ `The guards`

GIVEN act IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the brief allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `ledger records Bob's purchase`         THEN `dinner is open now` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
    WHEN `ledger records Bob's cancellation`     THEN NOT (`dinner is open now` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`))
    WHEN `Messages delivers the message`         THEN (RECALL Messages's `message`) EQUALS JUST `in transit`
    WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS planning
    WHEN `Alice is done`                         THEN `Alice has bought or stopped` (RECALL Alice's `plan`)
    WHEN `Alice buys dinner` answered            THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS checked

§ `The arrangement`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the arrangement` MEANS
    COMMIT `dinner status record` IS opened
    HENCE `the evening`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the evening` MEANS
    PARTY World
    MAY   act PROVIDED `the brief allows` act
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE CONSIDER act
          WHEN `ledger records Bob's purchase` THEN
              COMMIT `dinner status record` IS taken
              HENCE RECORD Messages's `message` IS `in transit`
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `ledger records Bob's cancellation` THEN
              COMMIT `dinner status record` IS opened
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Messages delivers the message` THEN
              RECORD Messages's `message` IS delivered
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `belief` IS taken
              HENCE `Alice stops unless she has bought` (RECALL Alice's `plan`)
          WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN
              RECORD Alice's `belief` IS `the latest status` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS checked
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice is done` THEN `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice buys dinner` answered THEN
              IF NOT answered
              THEN `the evening`
              ELSE `the ledger answers the purchase` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
    LEST  FULFILLED

-- The ledger's answer, in one step, read off the latest status.
GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the ledger answers the purchase` MEANS
    IF `dinner is open now` `dinner status record`
    THEN COMMIT `dinners bought` IS `dinner for two`
         HENCE COMMIT `open at acceptance` IS `dinner is open now` `dinner status record`
         HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS bought
         HENCE `the evening`
    ELSE RECORD Alice's `belief` IS taken
         HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS stopped
         HENCE `the evening`

GIVEN plan IS A MAYBE Plan
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Alice stops unless she has bought` MEANS
    IF `Alice has bought or stopped` plan
    THEN `the evening`
    ELSE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS stopped
         HENCE `the evening`

§ `The latest status, by hand`

#ASSERT `the latest status` (LIST opened) EQUALS opened
#ASSERT `the latest status` (LIST opened, taken) EQUALS taken
#ASSERT `the latest status` (LIST opened, taken, opened) EQUALS opened
#ASSERT NOT (`dinner is open now` (LIST opened, taken))

§ `The trace`

-- The pair's history, then Alice's buy, as the default semantic guard
-- takes it. Official record: opened, taken, opened, dinner for two, open
-- at acceptance TRUE.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` AT 65100
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`         AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's cancellation`     AT 65190
    PARTY World DOES (`Alice buys dinner` TRUE)              AT 65220
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)
